From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo_avfoundation: layers, main-thread hops and observers

The layer side of the AVFoundation video output.

The output keeps a strong reference to the AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer it is
given through --wid, makes its timebase the layer's controlTimebase, and
adds a transparent subtitle layer above it in the same superlayer (or
inside it, with a warning, when it has none). Renderer calls go through
the layers' sampleBufferRenderer. Work that UIKit needs on the main thread
(geometry reads, layer creation, observers, recovery flushes and timebase
attachment) is done with synchronous hops that never wait for the player
core; the subtitle layer's frame copy and its queued flushes are
asynchronous.

Key-value observers on the host layer's bounds and contentsScale, and
observers of the app resigning and regaining active state, only raise a
flag and wake the video output. They are removed on the main thread before
any state they touch is freed.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with Vivid's earlier patches.

